course: dictionary
lesson: 3323
title: Evasion: avoiding and dodging
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Evasion means avoiding something you should do or face, like a question, a rule or a duty. The verb is evade, and the adjective is evasive. Read the words around the word to find its meaning.
explain: «Paying tax is a legal duty; tax evasion, illegally not paying, can mean fines or prison.» The words illegally, fines and prison are clues. Nobody is fined or sent to prison for something good, so tax evasion must be a wrong thing to do.
explain: Evasion can also mean escaping someone who is chasing you. «A criminal's evasion of the police took him across three rooftops.» He is running away from the police, so evasion means dodging them. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a criminal's dodging of the police" still makes sense.
fact: Evasion means avoiding something you should do or face.
fact: Tax evasion means illegally not paying the tax you owe, and it can lead to fines or prison.
fact: «If 1 in 10 people didn't pay, about 1 in every 10 pounds of tax would be missing.» This shows why tax evasion matters to everyone.
fact: Tax avoidance uses legal loopholes to pay less tax, but tax evasion is against the law.
fact: The verb evade means to avoid or escape, and the adjective evasive describes someone who avoids giving a straight answer.
exercise: «Paying tax is a legal duty; tax evasion, illegally not paying, can mean fines or prison.» What does tax evasion mean? | Paying tax early to be kind | *Illegally not paying the tax you owe | Buying things that have tax on them | Paying a fine for parking
exercise: The politician kept changing the subject instead of answering the question. Which word describes this? | Kindness | *Evasion | Excitement | Decoration
exercise: «Tax evasion, illegally not paying, can mean fines or prison.» What might happen to someone who commits tax evasion? | A medal | *Fines or prison | A holiday | A prize
test: «A criminal's evasion of the police took him across three rooftops.» What does evasion mean here? | Telling the police the truth | *Escaping or dodging someone who is chasing you | Building a wall | Helping the police with a case
test: Which of these is an example of tax evasion? | Paying your tax on time every year | Filling in a tax form carefully | *Deliberately not paying tax you owe, which is against the law | Asking an adviser how to pay the right amount
exam: Which sentence uses evasion correctly? | The evasion of the shop was closed | Her evasion was tall and blue | Evasion she ran quickly to the shop | *Her evasion of the question made the reporters suspicious
